{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465819-is-santa-easterbunny-tooth-fairy-real-in-the-wod","id":1465819,"title":"Is Santa/EasterBunny/Tooth Fairy real in the WOD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-29T13:31:58-07:00","id":1465819,"title":"Is Santa/EasterBunny/Tooth Fairy real in the WOD?","content":"Belief shapes the consensus in the WoD... there are A LOT of children in the world who believe in Santa, the Easter Bunny, the Tooth Fairy etc... plus you have the tacit approval of adults in this belief and then all the movies about said beings... so would that mean theres enough consensus on them to make them real?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T14:20:28-07:00","id":1465828,"title":"","content":"Yes, and the Void Engineers assigned to keep them in check have one of the most frustrating jobs in the entire Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T14:24:12-07:00","id":1465829,"title":"","content":"Santa is a marauder. At least there\u2019s a marauder who bears a striking resemblance to him who\u2019s false reality is that the World of Darkness is a genuinely good place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T15:14:00-07:00","id":1465838,"title":"","content":"That belief gets deconstructed by logic in due time. If convincing children of nonsense were an effective strategy for injecting things into the Consensus, a lot of Cabals would be trying to produce shows for kids. Then again, the Syndicate has Media Control for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T08:11:06-07:00","id":1465897,"title":"","content":"The tellurian or reality in the world of darkness is not entirely shaped by consensus. Rather, it's the result of the push between the consensus and the world pillars (the hypothetical &quot;fixed&quot; metaphysical rules of reality that limit how it can be shaped, to my knowledge no mage has been able to figure them out) With that said, for me the characters that you mention do exist in the world of darkness as umbral entities or spirits that sporadically manifest in the material world when the belief in them becomes strong enough. (Which causes no end of headaches for the Union, good thing that their manifestations are few and far between) Then again, a crafty mage could take their role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 10-30-2021, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T08:30:02-07:00","id":1465901,"title":"","content":"And at this point, let me point out that vampires, werewolves, ghosts, and goblins don't exist in the world of Darkness because people believe they do; their existence are among the aforementioned pillars of reality. That said, check out Gods and Monsters: there are a few niches in there that could be filled by the likes of Santa Claus for the Easter Bunny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T11:14:35-07:00","id":1465929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mezlabor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465819-is-santa-easterbunny-tooth-fairy-real-in-the-wod#post1465819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A LOT of children in the world who believe in Santa, the Easter Bunny, the Tooth Fairy etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>There is not.<br /> <br /> All those legends are local, no matter how much some people delude themselves. They are inconsistent at best and outright non-existent in so many places with huge populations.<br /> <br /> Have you ever studied how their narratives change, if they even exist, across the world?<br /> <br /> Sure, Hollywood guarantees that everyone recognizes the US tropes for them and some people adopt them no matter where. But for most of the world's children it don't go beyond character recognition, as any other cartoon character. The legends that move them are completely local.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T13:32:36-07:00","id":1465940,"title":"","content":"Additionally, when it comes to the World of Darkness, and even more so with Mage, one needs to define &quot;real.&quot;<br /> <br /> If they exist as Umbrood, as there's a whole class of Umbrood that are spirits of human beliefs, is that real?<br /> <br /> If they exist as a form of bygone or similar unique entity that is unclear if they were formed by said beliefs or if they've taken on the forms of those characters to have enough power to stay in the material plane even if they don't actually do all the legends, are they real?<br /> <br /> Is the aforementioned Marauder Santa real?<br /> <br /> There's lots of ways that things can <b>exist</b> in the WoD. Whether that means the human beliefs of them are &quot;real&quot; is an entirely different issue. Also, as noted by monteparnas, common in Western culture is not the same as Consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T07:34:15-07:00","id":1466283,"title":"","content":"I also think it is very fitting for Mage if there is bleed over between various instances of the same character or entity. That is to say, Santa the Umbrood, Santa the Avatar, and Santa the Marauder are separate entities, but it works quite well if they sometimes act like they are the same entity. The blurred line drives the point that classifications aren't as clear cut as we think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T07:48:00-07:00","id":1466284,"title":"","content":"Also, note that with the right combination of Merits and Backgrounds, it's possible for Santa the Avatar to simultaneously be Santa the Umbrood or even Santa the Bygone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T12:29:06-07:00","id":1466314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465819-is-santa-easterbunny-tooth-fairy-real-in-the-wod?p=1466283#post1466283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think it is very fitting for Mage if there is bleed over between various instances of the same character or entity. That is to say, Santa the Umbrood, Santa the Avatar, and Santa the Marauder are separate entities, but it works quite well if they sometimes act like they are the same entity. The blurred line drives the point that classifications aren't as clear cut as we think.</div> </div> </div> </div>The advantage of some options like an Umbrood is that it doesn't really relies on the Consensus, local belief is more than enough.<br /> <br /> And it may also result in several entities that are &quot;aspects&quot; of them, as very different legends that are thought as the &quot;same&quot; entity nowadays may exist separately and yet answer to the same modern name.<br /> <br /> Especially with Santa, that is the most widespread of those in &quot;some&quot; form. The others, though, are far less ubiquitous even as different versions. The Tooth Fairy is the third more common and is already pretty much not that ubiquitous and much less consistent. The actual idea of a &quot;tooth fairy&quot; only exists in north Europe and some parts of England, and in the US. Historically even those regions have teeth-related superstitions more than fairy-tales.<br /> <br /> In romance-speaking Europe a similar legend sprang during the later half of the 19th century, but it is a magical rat or mouse, not a fairy, and even then it isn't as common as in the US and didn't reach every romance country. One I can say it never got to be popular in is Portugal, there and here in Brazil we don't have this legend except as an occasional borrowing from Hollywood. It isn't a thing in the rest of the world, although those teeth rituals are pretty common, consisting generally in burying or throwing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T15:20:44-07:00","id":1466346,"title":"","content":"I once read an adventure for Changeling the Dreaming (sorry, can't remember where, but I believe it was one of the magazines) where PCs travel to the North Pole and there meet Santa and Jack Frost. I still try to find it cause I liked the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-02-2021, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}